MotionScrap Integration for Motion Photo Video Merge

1. Introduction

Gallery currently provides a feature that creates a single video from multiple Motion Photos.

The existing implementation is built on top of the Story pipeline and uses MotionPhotoUtil APIs to extract video clips and estimate valid video ranges through "getOverlappingSection()".

While the current solution guarantees compatibility across different devices and video formats, all clips are transcoded before being merged. This results in unnecessary processing overhead for many Motion Photo scenarios.

This document proposes integrating MotionScrap as an optimized merge engine that minimizes transcoding while preserving compatibility with the existing workflow.

---

