Advantages

- Mature implementation
- Handles various video formats
- Consistent output behavior

Limitations

All clips are always transcoded regardless of format compatibility.

This leads to:

- Increased processing time
- High CPU utilization
- Additional battery consumption
- Potential quality degradation caused by re-encoding

---

3. Motivation

Motion Photos are typically captured within a short period of time and often share similar video characteristics:

- Same codec
- Same resolution
- Same frame rate
- Same color format

For these clips, transcoding is not required.

However, Motion Photos may also differ depending on:

- Device model
- Camera configuration
- HDR mode
- Software version
- Recording settings

As a result, a direct merge approach cannot be applied universally.

The objective is therefore:

«Transcode only when necessary.»

Instead of forcing all clips through the same transcoding pipeline, MotionScrap identifies compatible clips and processes them through the most efficient path.

---

4. Proposed Solution

MotionScrap introduces a hybrid processing model.

Before merging, MotionScrap analyzes all input clips and determines how each segment should be processed.

High-Level Flow

Motion Photos
