 │ Transfer   │ Transition  │ Transcode  │
 └────────────┴─────────────┴────────────┘
                     │
                     ▼
                   Muxer
                     │
                     ▼
                Output Video

---

5. Format Analysis

MotionScrap inspects the following properties for each clip:

- Video codec
- Resolution
- Frame rate
- Color format
- HDR metadata
- Rotation metadata

The analysis is used to determine a target format and identify compatible clip groups.

Example:

Clip| Format
A| H264 1080p 30fps
B| H264 1080p 30fps
C| H264 1080p 30fps
D| HEVC 1080p 30fps

Target format:

H264 1080p 30fps

In this case, clips A, B and C can be transferred directly while only clip D requires transcoding.

---

6. Processing Paths

6.1 Transfer

Used when a clip already matches the target format.

Processing:

- Read samples
- Adjust timestamps
- Write directly to output

Characteristics:

- No decoding
- No encoding
- No quality loss

---

6.2 Transition

Used for transition effects between adjacent clips.

Examples:

- Cross fade
- Dissolve
- Fade in / fade out

Processing:

- Decode required frames
- Generate transition frames
- Encode transition segment

Only the transition region requires rendering and encoding.

---

6.3 Transcode

Used when a clip differs from the target format.

Examples:

- Different codec
- Different resolution
- Different frame rate
- HDR mismatch

Processing:

- Decode
- Convert format
- Encode to target format

The converted segment is then merged with transfer and transition outputs.

---

7. Thread Architecture

MotionScrap uses dedicated worker threads to process different workloads independently.

Transfer Thread

Responsibilities:

- Sample reading
- Timestamp adjustment
- Sample transfer

Characteristics:

- Lightweight
- I/O intensive

---

Transition Thread

Responsibilities:

- Transition rendering
- Frame composition
- Effect generation

Characteristics:

- Compute intensive
- Independent from transfer processing

---

Transcode Thread

Responsibilities:

- Decode
- Format conversion
- Encode

Characteristics:

- Most expensive processing stage
- Triggered only when required

---

8. Integration with Existing Components

MotionScrap reuses existing MotionPhotoUtil functionality.

MotionPhotoUtil

Used for:

- Motion Photo parsing
- Metadata extraction
- Video clip extraction

getOverlappingSection()

Used for:

- Estimating valid video ranges
- Determining overlapping sections between clips

No changes are required to existing APIs.

